Regional Market Insights
•	Asia-Pacific: Dominates 58% of global consumption, driven by China and India's intensive agriculture. Coal-based production remains prevalent in China despite environmental pressures.
•	North America: Stable shale gas supplies support cost-competitive production, though the region remains a net importer to meet agricultural demand.
•	Middle East: Leverages abundant low-cost natural gas, with Qatar and Saudi Arabia operating world-scale export-oriented plants.
•	Europe: Focuses on premium urea variants with inhibitors to comply with environmental regulations.
•	Africa: Emerging production hubs in Nigeria and Egypt aim to reduce import dependency amidst growing agricultural demands.
